Keep a shared costs as an empty list of whole numbers.
For every slot from 0 to 200.
Place -1 into costs.

Keep a shared base as 0.
Keep a shared degree as 0.
Keep a shared reachpower as 0.
Keep a shared downcost as 0.
Set base to 3.
To grow with value (a whole number).
Set degree to 2.
Set reachpower to base times base.
Repeat while reachpower is less than value.
Set reachpower to reachpower times base.
Add 1 to degree.

To settle with value (a whole number).
The plusway is value times 2 minus 1.
The minusway is 2 times (base minus value).
Set item value of costs to plusway.
If minusway is less than plusway, set item value of costs to minusway.

To reach with value (a whole number).
If item value of costs is at least 0, return.
If value is 0, set item 0 of costs to 0, return.
If value is 1, set item 1 of costs to 2, return.
If base is at least value, Settle with value, return.
Grow with value.
The savedpower is reachpower.
The saveddegree is degree.
The spread is savedpower minus value.
The lower is savedpower divided by base.
Set downcost to 1000000.
If spread is less than value, Reach with spread.
If spread is less than value, set downcost to saveddegree plus item spread of costs.
The firstcost is downcost.
Reach with value minus lower.
The upcost is saveddegree minus 1 plus item (value minus lower) of costs.
Set item value of costs to upcost.
If firstcost is less than upcost, set item value of costs to firstcost.

Reach with 19.
The answer is item 19 of costs minus 1.
Show answer.
